SUMMARY:The Bush Farmhouse Restaurant ~ Featured on “Diners\, Drive-ins 
 and Dives”
DESCRIPTION:Senior Singles Fun Bunch\n**The Bush Farmhouse offers South Af
 rican-inspired food and drink. Their dishes are prepared with fresh produc
 e from their on-site garden and greenhouse.**\n\n**This restaurant caught 
 my eye for it was recently featured in an episode of Guy Fieri’s “Dine
 rs\, Drive-ins\, and Dives” in May 2026. The restaurant is quite unique.
  They have quaint decor plus a small outdoor menagerie of rescue animals ~
  miniature donkeys\, ducks\, chickens\, pigs\, etc. 🫏 🐓 🐖 I thoug
 ht it would be fun to check it out so come join me!**\n\n**MENU:** **www.b
 ushfarmhouse.com**\n**They offer vegetarian and vegan options. Also cockta
 ils\, beer & wines. 🍹🍺 🍷**\n\n**TABLE RESERVATIONS: 12:30 PM**\n*
 *The max number of attendees the restaurant will allow me is 16. So RSVP n
 ow!**\n\n**PETS: 🐶** **Allowed on outdoor covered and uncovered patio a
 reas.**\n\n**GIFT-SHOP:** **They carry their own Bush Farmhouse merchandis
 e.**\n\n**PARKING: 🅿️** **On-site parking available.**\n\n**NOTE:** *
 *The restaurant is located only a few blocks (2-minute walk) from downtown
  Black Mountain so after you eat (or even before) you might want to check 
 out the cool shops.**\n\n**LAKE TOMAHAWK PARK:** **This public park might 
 interest you while you’re in the area. It’s only 1/2 mile from downtow
 n Black Mountain. It’s 16.3 acre and has walking trails\, a playground\,
  a fishing pier\, and\, of course\, the 8.9 acre scenic lake.**\n\n**So co
 me join me for lunch at the Bush Farmhouse Restaurant and then go stroll d
 owntown while you’re in the area or go check out Lake Tomahawk!**\n\n**Q
 UESTIONS/CONCERNS:**\n**Shae.kemerer@aol.com**\n**(828)699-8180 (Text or c
 all)**
